course: dictionary
lesson: 6164
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to choose the right one. «Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.» Here, a mineral is a natural solid found in rocks and the ground, like quartz or gold.
explain: «Fruit and veg of different colours give different vitamins and minerals.» The words vitamins and fruit are the clues. Here, a mineral is a substance our bodies need in small amounts to stay healthy, like calcium for bones.
explain: Mineral water is water from a natural spring with minerals dissolved in it. In British and Irish English, asking for a mineral can mean asking for a fizzy soft drink. Always check the clues: is the sentence about rocks, food, water or a shop?
fact: A mineral is a natural, non-living solid found in rocks and the ground, like quartz, salt, gold or iron ore.
fact: Our bodies need minerals in small amounts to stay healthy.
fact: «Calcium» is a mineral that keeps our bones strong; milk and cheese have it.
fact: «Iron» is a mineral in red meat, beans and spinach, and our blood needs it.
fact: Plants take minerals from the soil through their roots.
exercise: «Most gems are minerals that grew as crystals deep in the Earth.» In this sentence, a mineral is | A type of tap water | A fizzy soft drink | *A natural solid found in rocks | A kind of vitamin
exercise: Jay asks for a mineral in a Dublin café and gets a fizzy lemonade. What does mineral mean here? | A rock from a cave | A healthy food | *A fizzy soft drink | A glass of spring water
exercise: «Milk and cheese give us calcium, which keeps our bones strong.» Calcium is | A rock | A fizzy drink | A type of mountain | *A mineral our body needs to stay healthy
test: «Red meat, beans and spinach give us iron, a mineral our blood needs.» What is a mineral in this sentence? | Water from a tap | A shiny crystal from a cave | A kind of mountain | *A substance our body needs in small amounts
test: «Mineral water comes from a natural spring.» What does mineral water mean? | *Water from a natural spring with minerals dissolved in it | Sea water from the beach | Rain collected in a bucket | Water boiled in a kettle
exam: «Old shark teeth are turned black by minerals over a long time.» Which meaning of mineral fits best? | A healthy food like a banana | *A natural substance found in rocks and the ground | A fizzy soft drink | A kind of spring water
